PARITY (web RouteDisplay.tsx -> native, no scope narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web component is a generic, purely props-driven "From -> To" / "round trip" / single-location /
"No location data" line + optional lucide MapPin. Its ONLY hook is useTranslation; there is NO data
fetch, so it has NO loading/empty/error/stale/offline DATA states (same shape as the accepted
PlaybackSpeedMenu 0097 precedent). Every render branch the source has is reproduced:

  web branch (RouteDisplay.tsx)                          -> native (RouteDisplayContent)
  !startLabel && !endLabel  ("No location data", dim)    -> .noLocation(text:)          [dim 0.6]
  isRoundTrip && isExplicitSingle  (only start)          -> .single(start:)             [no suffix]
  isRoundTrip && !isExplicitSingle ("{s} ↻ round trip")  -> .roundTrip(start:phrase:)   [suffix dim]
  else  ("{s} -> {e}", per-side fallback)                -> .fromTo(start:end:)
  endpointLabel: trim addr | "📍 lat, lon" (toFixed 2) | nil  -> RouteDisplayLogic.endpointLabel
  haversineMeters(R=6_371_000, min(1,..) clamp)          -> RouteDisplayLogic.haversineMeters
  roundTripThresholdM=100 default, showIcon=true         -> same defaults
  testId hook                                            -> accessibilityIdentifier

Data sources: useTranslation only -> P1/S10 facade RouteDisplayStrings (table "RouteDisplay").
Shared components used by source: none. Charts/maps used by source: none.
i18n keys extracted from source (2): route.noLocationData="No location data";
route.roundTrip="round trip" -> both in RouteDisplay.strings, resolved via the facade (0 hardcoded
English in code paths). Tokens: P1/S9 generated Tokens.swift (Color.TS/Font.TS/TSSpacing/TSRadius);
